{
  "_comment": [
    "#538 — the two-sided contract fixture for the workbench's 'Copy as Bowire CLI' export.",
    "",
    "READ BY TWO TESTS, ON PURPOSE:",
    "  * tests/Kuestenlogik.Bowire.Tests/wwwroot-js/cli-export.test.mjs replays each `ctx`",
    "    through wwwroot/js/cli-export.js and asserts `argv`, `rendered` and `notes`.",
    "  * tests/Kuestenlogik.Bowire.Tests/Cli/CliExportGrammarTests.cs feeds the SAME `argv`",
    "    (minus the leading 'bowire' / 'call' tokens) through the real System.CommandLine",
    "    `call` command and asserts zero parse errors.",
    "",
    "So: rename or drop a flag on `bowire call` and the C# side goes red; change the",
    "generator and the JS side goes red. A 'Copy as CLI' button that emits a command the",
    "CLI rejects is worse than no button, and this pair is what prevents it.",
    "",
    "Keep at least one scenario per emitted flag (--url, --protocol, --stream, -d, -H, --var):",
    "a flag no scenario exercises can still be renamed silently.",
    "",
    "`vars` seeds the test's substituteVars stub. `keepVars` drives the Code tab's",
    "'Keep {{variables}}' pill. `rendered` is the POSIX flavour."
  ],
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "scenario": "grpc-unary-body-and-header",
      "ctx": {
        "serverUrl": "http://localhost:5001",
        "service": "fleet.FleetService",
        "method": "GetShip",
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "httpPath": "",
        "bodyJson": "{\"id\":101}",
        "bodyJsonRaw": "{\"id\":101}",
        "metadata": { "authorization": "Bearer t0k3n" },
        "metadataRaw": { "authorization": "Bearer t0k3n" },
        "source": "grpc",
        "protocolId": "grpc",
        "serverStreaming": false,
        "clientStreaming": false,
        "messages": ["{\"id\":101}"],
        "authKind": "bearer",
        "authLocation": ""
      },
      "argv": ["bowire", "call", "--url", "grpc@http://localhost:5001", "fleet.FleetService/GetShip", "-d", "{\"id\":101}", "-H", "authorization: Bearer t0k3n"],
      "rendered": "bowire call \\\n  --url grpc@http://localhost:5001 \\\n  fleet.FleetService/GetShip \\\n  -d '{\"id\":101}' \\\n  -H 'authorization: Bearer t0k3n'",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "scenario": "grpc-server-streaming-no-body",
      "ctx": {
        "serverUrl": "http://localhost:5001",
        "service": "fleet.FleetService",
